.TH GEMSERVE 8
.SH NAME
gemserve \- Gemini server driven by a 9P control file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gemserve
.RI [ ctlfile ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gemserve
runs in the Purgatorio guest.  It follows an append-only control file,
synthesizes a gemtext page from the commands it reads, and serves that
page over TLS 1.3 or TLS 1.2 on the same port.
.PP
Each connection is peeked at before the handshake.  If the ClientHello
offers TLS 1.3 (supported_versions 0x0304, X25519, and
TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256), the handshake runs in Dis using
.IR tls (2)'s
.B gcmseal
,
.B gcmopen
and
.B sign
primitives and
.IR mono (2)'s
X25519.  Otherwise the bytes already read are handed back to the
kernel with
.B tls->acceptpre
and BearSSL performs a TLS 1.2 handshake.  Both paths serve the same
page.
The default control file is
.BR /n/host/gem/ctl ,
a 9P mount of a file on the host; the guest only reads it.
.PP
The control language is line oriented:
.TP
.BI title " text"
Set the page title.
.TP
.BI text " line"
Append one line of gemtext.
.TP
.BI set " key value"
Set or replace a data key; the value may contain spaces.
.TP
.BI del " key"
Remove a key.
.TP
.B clear
Reset the title, text and keys.
.PP
The page is regenerated for every request; it contains the title, the
text lines, a data list and the count of applied commands.  A missing
control file leaves the page empty but the listener running.
.PP
The certificate and key are kept in
.B /keydb/gemini.cert
and
.BR /keydb/gemini.key .
On first start,
.B gemserve
mints a self-signed ECDSA P-256 leaf with
.IR tls (2);
later starts reuse it, so the trust-on-first-use fingerprint is stable.
.PP
.B gemserve
listens on TCP port 1965 on all interfaces.  The guest needs an
address on the host tap (for example
.B ip=10.0.0.2
and
.B mask=255.255.255.0
in
.BR /n/host/net.conf )
before clients can reach it.
.SH FILES
.TF /keydb/gemini.cert
.TP
.B /n/host/gem/ctl
append-only control file, written by the host
.TP
.B /keydb/gemini.cert
leaf certificate, DER
.TP
.B /keydb/gemini.key
ECDSA P-256 private scalar
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/gemserve.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR tls (2),
.IR init (8)
.SH BUGS
The TLS 1.3 handshake does not send session tickets or support
resumption, and it requires the client to offer X25519 and an ECDSA
P-256 signature.  Connections are served one at a time; a client that
connects and sends nothing blocks the listener until it is killed.
.PP
The control file is opened once at start; if it is absent the server
does not retry.  The control state is a log: it is replayed from the
beginning on each start, so a long-lived log is read in full.  There is
one page and no per-URL routing.
